# Re-route imports on refactor

When moving a symbol (constant, type, function, class) to a new module:

- Update every import site to the new location.
- Search all workspace repos for consumers before deciding a re-export is needed.

Never leave a compatibility re-export at the old location (`export { X }`, `export { X } from "./new.js"`, or `export * from` solely to preserve the old path). Stale re-exports create ambiguous barrel exports and hide the real module boundary.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — symbol moved to token-types.ts, old module still re-exports it
export { NON_STRATEGY_PHANTOM_TOKEN_TYPES };

// ✅ GOOD — consumers import from the new home
import { NON_STRATEGY_PHANTOM_TOKEN_TYPES } from "../../base/token-types.js";
```

If there are truly external consumers that cannot be updated in this change, ask the user instead of silently keeping the re-export.
